  "note": "Thumb takes half/quarter states for pinching. Holes 6 and 7 are double on most baroque instruments, drawn as a twin: one ring with a large (a) and a small (b) hole; treat h6a/h6b and h7a/h7b as one hole on a German-fingering or single-hole instrument.",
